name o3-03-ingress-1
timeout 400
time 1973-10-06T12:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN O3, SORTIE 3 OF 10 - YOM KIPPUR 1973: GROUND ATTACK IN CONTESTED AIRSPACE.
# THE INGRESS LADDER, AND IT IS THE FILE THAT LICENSES EVERY OTHER GEOMETRY IN THIS CAMPAIGN.
# CONTROL: none - it carries its OWN control inside it, three aircraft one fact apart, in the shape
# w4-07-cap-intercept.fbm uses.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/o3-yom-kippur-1973.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
#
# THE SUBSTITUTION AND ITS DIRECTION (stated in every O3 file): the MiG-29 stands in for the MiG-17 /
# Su-7 / Su-20 / MiG-21 of 6 October 1973, whose own catalogue rows are ALPHA and may not answer a
# campaign question. It makes the ATTACKER materially STRONGER than history. A bad O3 result therefore
# says more than the record did; a good one says nothing. HERE THE DIRECTION BITES HARDEST: the defect
# this sortie measures is the MiG-29's, and the subsonic types it stands in for had a different one.
#
# WHY THIS SORTIE EXISTS. Every other O3 striker spawns ~6 km from its aim point. That is a short final
# by any doctrine and it looks like an author's convenience, so W4's rule applies - an absence that
# decides a result belongs in the mission file, PRICED. The price is this file.
#
# THE MECHANISM, and it is an airframe property with a source, not a delivery property. This MiG-29's
# yaw channel is measured OFF (doc/modules/mig29/module.md gap 4i), so on any straight leg it acquires a
# standing CROSS-TRACK offset that saturates near 90-100 m. It was measured once before, on the Payerne
# rig: `missions/mig29-opt-stability.fbm` gives aimAcrossM 44.99 m on a 6 km final and 92.22 m on a
# 12 km one, and the F-16 flying the identical 12 km line comes out at 8.6 m - a factor of 11 that has
# nothing to do with the OPT director and everything to do with the airframe.
# WHAT THAT DOES TO A CAMPAIGN: a FAB-500 finishes a `target_soft` out to 68.4 m [DERIVED, o3-01's
# header]. 90 m of cross-track is therefore not "less accurate", it is A MISS, and it arrives after
# ~10 km of straight flight. The anchor's own opening strike was 220 aircraft flying coordinated
# approach routes; in this tree such an approach cannot hit.
#
# THE THREE RUNS, and only ONE thing changes between any two of them - the length of the final leg:
#   y3a   6.02 km final   spawn 32.55700 -> aim 32.62000, 30.80000 N
#   y3b  12.00 km final   spawn 32.49450 -> aim 32.62000, 30.82000 N
#   y3c  24.00 km final   spawn 32.36900 -> aim 32.62000, 30.84000 N
# Same altitude (300 m), same commanded speed (450 kt), same store (fab500), same target class
# (`target_soft`), same clock, same egress shape. The three aim points sit 2.22 km apart in latitude, so
# no bomb's fragment field can reach a neighbour (68.4 m against 2 223 m) and the three deliveries are
# independent. Scale: 1 deg lon at 30.80 N = 95 619 m, 1 deg lat = 111 132 m [DERIVED].
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: HOW LONG A RUN-IN CAN THIS AIRFRAME FLY AND STILL PUT A FREE-FALL BOMB
# INSIDE A SOFT POSITION'S LETHAL RADIUS? The answer is a length in kilometres, and it is the number
# that decides whether O3's anchor - a coordinated 220-aircraft strike flying real approach routes - is
# flyable in this tree at all.
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-30, --elev const, campaign step 3, fingerprint 12edfcf6f8e45792, exit 3):
#   unit  final     aimErrM   aimLongM   aimAcrossM   openLoopAlongM   devSpeedMs   position
#   y3a    6.02 km    66.39     -45.52      +48.34        -70.33         -1.476     DESTROYED t = 26.2
#   y3b   12.00 km    88.58     +15.44      +87.23         -9.92         -0.073     DEGRADED, alive
#   y3c   24.00 km    94.05     +24.30      +90.85         -0.99         +0.000     DEGRADED, alive
#   -> THE LADDER IS MONOTONE IN CROSS-TRACK AND IT CROSSES THE KILL RADIUS BETWEEN 6 AND 12 KM.
#      48.3 -> 87.2 -> 90.9 m of cross error against a 68.4 m radius: ONE KILL OF THREE, and the two
#      that miss are the two that flew a realistic approach. y3b and y3c both land inside the DEGRADE
#      threshold (fluxJm2 1 717 and 1 553 against 1 200) and outside the FAIL one (2 800), so the
#      positions are hurt and keep standing - which in this tree is the same as untouched.
#   -> AND THE TWO ERROR TERMS TRADE, EXACTLY OPPOSITELY. The 6 km run has the WORST procedure error
#      (openLoopAlongM -70.3 m, because the plan is frozen 4.3 s before release on an aircraft still
#      1.476 m/s off its planned speed) and the BEST cross error; the 24 km run has a procedure error of
#      -0.99 m - a stabilised aircraft gives a frozen plan nothing to get wrong, and devSpeedMs is zero
#      to three decimals - and the WORST cross error. THE DIRECTOR GETS 71x BETTER WITH LEG LENGTH AND
#      THE AIRFRAME GETS 1.9x WORSE, and the airframe wins because only IT is compared against a lethal
#      radius: 70 m of range error still kills a 20 m installation, 90 m of cross error does not.
#   -> SO O3's 6 KM FINALS ARE NOT A CONVENIENCE, THEY ARE THE ONLY GEOMETRY IN WHICH THIS CAMPAIGN CAN
#      SCORE A KILL AT ALL, and the campaign says so here instead of implying it nine times.
#   -> AND THE OTHER HALF OF THE RUN-IN FINDING IS THE TURN, measured as attribution run A2 (four
#      aircraft, same 6.02 km final, dog-leg angle the only variable):
#          0.0 deg -> across +48.3 m, KILL      +5.3 deg -> +229.7 m      -5.3 deg -> -131.0 m
#         +10.5 deg -> +401.1 m
#      A THREE-POINT FIT GIVES across = 48.3 m + 33.9 m PER DEGREE OF DOG-LEG [DERIVED], so the largest
#      turn this airframe may make inside its final and still kill a soft position is
#      (68.4 - 48.3) / 33.9 = 0.59 DEGREES. That is why every O3 striker's aim point sits on its own
#      spawn latitude, and it is a harder constraint than the leg length this file measures.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT MEASURE, named rather than glossed: it does not separate the yaw channel from the
# guidance's own cross-track hold, because both act on the same axis and neither is separately
# observable from a mission file. `doc/modules/mig29/module.md` gap 4i owns that split.
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the EXPECTED shape - two of the three `kill unit` objectives are
# never met, so nothing concludes and the clock runs out. THIS IS A MEASURING RIG in the shape of
# `mig29-opt-stability.fbm`: no single row of the table above proves anything, and y3tb / y3tc
# surviving is the RESULT and not a failure. THE MEASUREMENT is the three `stores DELIVERY` lines read
# as a table beside the three `director DIRECTOR_RELEASE` lines, plus the three `damage DAMAGE` lines'
# `fluxJm2` against the 1 200 / 2 800 thresholds. exit 0 would mean all three killed and would
# contradict `mig29-opt-stability.fbm`; exit 2 would be a defect.

unit y3a
  module mig29
  team hostile
  spawn 30.80000 32.55700 300 90.0 450       # 6.02 km final
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_emission off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 fab500
  set store 6 fab500
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode opt
  wp 30.80000 32.62000 300 450
  wp 30.86000 32.30000 300 450
  objective kill unit y3ta
  objective survive

unit y3ta
  module target_soft
  team friendly
  spawn 30.80000 32.62000 ground 90.0 0

unit y3b
  module mig29
  team hostile
  spawn 30.82000 32.49450 300 90.0 450       # THE ONE CHANGED LINE: 12.00 km final
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_emission off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 fab500
  set store 6 fab500
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode opt
  wp 30.82000 32.62000 300 450
  wp 30.88000 32.30000 300 450
  objective kill unit y3tb
  objective survive

unit y3tb
  module target_soft
  team friendly
  spawn 30.82000 32.62000 ground 90.0 0

unit y3c
  module mig29
  team hostile
  spawn 30.84000 32.36900 300 90.0 450       # THE ONE CHANGED LINE: 24.00 km final
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_emission off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 fab500
  set store 6 fab500
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode opt
  wp 30.84000 32.62000 300 450
  wp 30.90000 32.30000 300 450
  objective kill unit y3tc
  objective survive

unit y3tc
  module target_soft
  team friendly
  spawn 30.84000 32.62000 ground 90.0 0
